            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0116" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/933: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Capetown</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-24T20:00:00-04:00">January 24, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Reference your 24, January 18, 5 p.m. Treasury asks that Financial Secretary
                    be informed that no monetary conference has as yet been scheduled. Part of the
                    Russian delegation of experts has arrived for informal technical discussions of
                    the same bilateral and preliminary character as those previously held with the
                    technical experts of other United Nations including the Union. You will be
                    promptly informed of any decision to hold a formal conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
